{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>This time.</b> That is, now a woman came from the man, but from here onward it is not so — rather, the man comes from the woman." "<b>This time, bone of my bones.</b> Rashi: this teaches that the man lay with every animal and beast, and his mind was not satisfied. One must say that they conceived before the man lay with them, for if you do not say so, they would be sterilized by the man's intercourse." "<b>Bone of my bones.</b> This creature is not like the rest of the creatures, which are from the earth and the water and the mire. And why is she different? In this the Holy One, blessed be He, intended that a man leave his father and his mother and cleave to his wife, and then they become one flesh — that is, his body is complete; therefore he pursues her, for she is from him, as though he were missing one of his limbs — as in the example 'and the tabernacle shall be one.' But animals, beasts, birds, and other creatures do not pursue so much, because they are not missing anything." "<b>To this shall be called woman.</b> As in the example 'for he is a young woman, a virgin.'" "<b>For from man she was taken.</b> But the females of other creatures were not taken from the males; therefore they are not named after the pattern of the male, as in 'males-goats, rams-ewes, bulls-cows, male donkeys-female donkeys.'" "<b>For from man she was taken.</b> She came forth from him, unlike the way other creatures are formed, so that she would not be available for relations with other men, but only to the partner of her covenant, who is her man, and she is his rib. And so it says: ודבק באשתו. Rabbi Chanina expounded: איש and אשה — if they merited to walk in a straight path, the two of them without adultery — HaShem is between them, for He divided His name and placed it between them. If they did not merit — אש אוכלתם, for HaShem removes His name from between them, and it is found אש and אש. And אשה is more potent than איש: the אש of a woman is harsh and swifter to consume and to exact retribution more than that of a man. What is the reason? This אש of a woman is apt to flame, for no letter of the [divine] name interrupts it, but it is joined together and is called אש. But that of a man — the letters do not combine, for the yod of the Name separates them. So it is taught in a Tannaic source, and so Rashi explained in tractate Sotah."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {5 "The phrase דרך הנוצרים literally means 'the way of those who are formed/created'; rendered as 'other creatures' for sense. The wordplay depends on the Hebrew letters of איש (man) and אשה (woman) and the divine name י-ה (yod-hei): א-י-ש / א-ש-ה contain the letters אש (fire), but only אשה keeps them adjacent without an intervening letter."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:02:47.468008986Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}